WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.839
Disability underwriting starts with the job, not the body.

00:00:03.839 --> 00:00:08.105
Insurers sort occupations into classes by the physical demands, the

00:00:08.105 --> 00:00:12.370
hazards and how easily a disabled worker could keep working.

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:17.489
An attorney or accountant falls in the best class, with access to

00:00:17.489 --> 00:00:22.608
true own-occupation definitions, the longest benefit periods and the highest issue limits.

00:00:22.608 --> 00:00:28.579
Rosa, an electrician, sits in a middle class: her work is physical and hazardous,

00:00:28.579 --> 00:00:34.551
so her definition may be modified, her benefit period shorter and her premium higher.

00:00:34.551 --> 00:00:39.670
Some occupations, such as commercial fishing or stunt work, are declined entirely.

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:41.546
The second pillar is income.

00:00:41.546 --> 00:00:44.549
The insurer asks for tax returns or pay

00:00:44.549 --> 00:00:47.176
stubs and applies issue and participation limits.

00:00:47.176 --> 00:00:52.430
The issue limit is the most benefit it will write; the participation limit is

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:57.309
the most total coverage from all sources, including group plans, it will allow.

00:00:57.309 --> 00:01:02.188
Both are expressed as a replacement ratio, commonly 60 to 70 percent of

00:01:02.188 --> 00:01:07.066
earned income at modest incomes, falling to 40 or 50 percent at high

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:11.195
incomes, because wealthier insureds have other resources and benefits are tax-free.

00:01:11.195 --> 00:01:16.074
Unearned income, such as rent or dividends, reduces the need and the limit.

00:01:16.074 --> 00:01:17.950
Too much coverage invites malingering.

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:19.320
Medical underwriting follows.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:25.711
The underwriter reviews the application, physician statements and test results from Lesson 12 for

00:01:25.711 --> 00:01:31.645
conditions likely to cause disability: back problems, mental health history, cardiovascular disease, diabetes.

00:01:31.645 --> 00:01:37.123
Hobbies such as piloting, racing or climbing may be excluded or rated.

00:01:37.123 --> 00:01:41.689
Lifestyle factors, including tobacco and alcohol use, affect the class.

00:01:41.689 --> 00:01:46.254
Financial stability matters too; a business with falling revenue signals

00:01:46.254 --> 00:01:50.819
a higher chance that a marginal disability becomes a claim.

00:01:50.819 --> 00:01:57.210
The underwriter weighs all of it against the occupation class to reach an offer.

00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:00.313
An applicant with a problem is rarely simply declined.

00:02:00.313 --> 00:02:05.139
The insurer can issue with a rated premium, charging more for the higher risk.

00:02:05.139 --> 00:02:08.931
It can attach an exclusion rider that removes claims caused by

00:02:08.931 --> 00:02:12.723
a named condition, such as Rosa’s shoulder, while covering everything else.

00:02:12.723 --> 00:02:16.171
It can issue modified benefits: a longer elimination period, a

00:02:16.171 --> 00:02:19.618
shorter benefit period or a lower monthly amount than requested.

00:02:19.618 --> 00:02:23.755
It can change the definition from own occupation to modified own occupation.

00:02:23.755 --> 00:02:27.892
These alternatives let the insurer say yes to most of the risk.

00:02:27.892 --> 00:02:29.960
A decline is the last resort.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:34.538
The underwriter reviews Rosa’s file: electrician, 6,000 dollars a month,

00:02:34.538 --> 00:02:39.117
a shoulder injury treated two years ago, no other coverage.

00:02:39.117 --> 00:02:44.611
The offer: 3,600 dollars a month, benefits to 65, 90-day elimination period,

00:02:44.611 --> 00:02:50.105
modified own-occupation definition because of her class, standard premium for the class,

00:02:50.105 --> 00:02:55.600
and an exclusion rider for the right shoulder for the first two

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:59.720
years, after which the insurer will reconsider on request.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:01.552
Theo explains each term.

00:03:01.552 --> 00:03:05.214
Rosa can accept, ask for the shoulder rider

00:03:05.214 --> 00:03:08.877
to be reviewed sooner, or decline the counteroffer.

00:03:08.877 --> 00:03:12.540
She accepts and signs the amendment at delivery.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:16.492
When a question describes a disability applicant, look for three things.

00:03:16.492 --> 00:03:19.726
The occupation tells you the class, the definition available

00:03:19.726 --> 00:03:22.601
and whether the risk is insurable at all.

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:25.475
The income tells you the maximum benefit through

00:03:25.475 --> 00:03:27.991
the replacement ratio, after subtracting other coverage.

00:03:27.991 --> 00:03:31.943
The medical and lifestyle facts tell you whether to expect a

00:03:31.943 --> 00:03:35.536
standard issue, a rating, an exclusion rider or a modification.

00:03:35.536 --> 00:03:40.567
Disability income coverage is an exception to the usual rules for comprehensive medical plans.

00:03:40.567 --> 00:03:44.160
An insurer can still use full underwriting for disability coverage.
